// else part of `k != 5` gives k == 5 (deleted); `k != 5 || v[k] > 0.0` evaluates v[k] in an ifz
// part, where k == 5 (deleted); j in [0, 7] after two break tests, then `if j == 7 { break }`
// leaves j != 7, so j <= 6 (w of 7 elements: deleted)
